              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "propinquus, propinqua, propinquum — \"near; a relative\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Multī propinquī ad nūptiās veniunt. Many relatives come to the wedding."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From prope — near. As a noun, propinquus or propinqua — a relative. English propinquity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "propinquus is built on prope \"near\" (Lewis & Short). English propinquity \"nearness\" comes from it."
            }
          ]
